  ],
  "equipment_type": "Power and energy meter",
  "applies_to": "Eaton (Cutler-Hammer) IQ meters and trip units with an RS-485 PONI Modbus card, read by a BASgatewayLX (LO/HI word order).",
  "summary": "Gateway profile for an Eaton RS-485 PONI: 106 Analog Inputs, 44 polled by default. It reads primary status and cause, phase, ground and neutral currents, voltages, peak current demands, real/reactive/apparent power, power factors and frequency; energy registers are unpolled.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "Built from Contemporary Controls' BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile Eaton_RS485_PONI_LO_HI_b_LX.csv; the profile maps the registers in the maker's Modbus register document (https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/EatonPONI.pdf).",
    "Object instances are the ones this profile assigns when it is loaded into the gateway. A site that edited or rebuilt the profile may use different instances.",
    "Only 44 of the 106 rows are flagged for polling in the profile; the rest are served only after you tick them in the gateway. Their descriptions say \"not polled by default\".",
    "The CSV has no read/write column: Analog/Binary Inputs are read-only and Analog/Binary Outputs are commandable (priority array), which is how the gateway maps them (access inferred). Descriptions give the Modbus register each object reads.",
    "Some names appear more than once in the profile as published (Frequency); they are kept as printed and told apart by instance."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile Eaton_RS485_PONI_LO_HI_b",
    "doc_number": "Eaton_RS485_PONI_LO_HI_b_LX.csv",
